\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S6}{\ignorespaces Sensitivity of estimated endophyte effects to exclusion of sites KER and SON, which were destroyed by deer and subsequently replanted in 2024. For each combination of vital rate (Trait), species, herbivory treatment (Access = herbivory-access plots, Exclusion = herbivore-exclusion plots), and precipitation (Precip., in mm; three values spanning each species' observed precipitation range), the table reports the posterior median and 90\% credible interval [Med.\ $\Delta $ (90\% CI)] and the posterior probability of a positive endophyte effect [P($\Delta >0$)] for the full dataset and for the dataset excluding KER and SON. The endophyte effect $\Delta $ is defined as Pr(S+) $-$ Pr(S-) for survival, or the analogous difference on the response scale (S+ $-$ S-) for growth, inflorescence production, and spikelet production. Spikelet production was not modeled for \textit  {A.\ hyemalis} because spikelets in this species were too numerous and small to count reliably (see Methods). Posterior estimates were nearly identical between the full dataset and the dataset excluding KER and SON across all species, vital rates, and herbivory treatments, indicating that the disturbance and replanting at these two sites did not meaningfully influence our conclusions.}}{9}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:sensitivity_KER_SON}{{S6}{9}{Sensitivity of estimated endophyte effects to exclusion of sites KER and SON, which were destroyed by deer and subsequently replanted in 2024. For each combination of vital rate (Trait), species, herbivory treatment (Access = herbivory-access plots, Exclusion = herbivore-exclusion plots), and precipitation (Precip., in mm; three values spanning each species' observed precipitation range), the table reports the posterior median and 90\% credible interval [Med.\ $\Delta $ (90\% CI)] and the posterior probability of a positive endophyte effect [P($\Delta >0$)] for the full dataset and for the dataset excluding KER and SON. The endophyte effect $\Delta $ is defined as Pr(S+) $-$ Pr(S-) for survival, or the analogous difference on the response scale (S+ $-$ S-) for growth, inflorescence production, and spikelet production. Spikelet production was not modeled for \textit {A.\ hyemalis} because spikelets in this species were too numerous and small to count reliably (see Methods). Posterior estimates were nearly identical between the full dataset and the dataset excluding KER and SON across all species, vital rates, and herbivory treatments, indicating that the disturbance and replanting at these two sites did not meaningfully influence our conclusions}{table.6}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S7}{\ignorespaces  Posterior summaries of $\Delta $ (S$+$ $-$ S$-$) for survival across precipitation quantiles (mm, 5\%, 25\%, 50\%, 75\%, 100\%) for each species and herbivore treatment. Positive median values indicate beneficial effects of symbionts; negative medians indicate costly effects. $P(\Delta >0)$ quantifies the strength of evidence: values near 1 indicate strong support for a benefit, values near 0 indicate strong support for a cost, and values near 0.5 indicate little or no consistent effect. Herbivore treatment: Exclusion = herbivores excluded; Access = herbivores had access. }}{13}{table.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:delta_summary_surv_quantiles}{{S7}{13}{Posterior summaries of $\Delta $ (S$+$ $-$ S$-$) for survival across precipitation quantiles (mm, 5\%, 25\%, 50\%, 75\%, 100\%) for each species and herbivore treatment. Positive median values indicate beneficial effects of symbionts; negative medians indicate costly effects. $P(\Delta >0)$ quantifies the strength of evidence: values near 1 indicate strong support for a benefit, values near 0 indicate strong support for a cost, and values near 0.5 indicate little or no consistent effect. Herbivore treatment: Exclusion = herbivores excluded; Access = herbivores had access}{table.caption.7}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S8}{\ignorespaces Posterior summaries of $\Delta $ ($S^+ - S^-$) for growth across precipitation quantiles (mm, 5\%, 25\%, 50\%, 75\%, 100\%) for each species and herbivore treatment. Positive median values indicate beneficial effects of symbionts; negative medians indicate costly effects. $P(\Delta >0)$ quantifies the strength of evidence: values near 1 indicate strong support for a benefit, values near 0 indicate strong support for a cost, and values near 0.5 indicate little or no consistent effect.}}{14}{table.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:delta_summary_grow}{{S8}{14}{Posterior summaries of $\Delta $ ($S^+ - S^-$) for growth across precipitation quantiles (mm, 5\%, 25\%, 50\%, 75\%, 100\%) for each species and herbivore treatment. Positive median values indicate beneficial effects of symbionts; negative medians indicate costly effects. $P(\Delta >0)$ quantifies the strength of evidence: values near 1 indicate strong support for a benefit, values near 0 indicate strong support for a cost, and values near 0.5 indicate little or no consistent effect}{table.caption.8}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S9}{\ignorespaces Posterior summaries of $\Delta $ ($S^+ - S^-$) for inflorescence production across precipitation quantiles (mm, 5\%, 25\%, 50\%, 75\%, 100\%) for each species and herbivore treatment. Positive median values indicate beneficial effects of symbionts; negative medians indicate costly effects. $P(\Delta >0)$ quantifies the strength of evidence: values near 1 indicate strong support for a benefit, values near 0 indicate strong support for a cost, and values near 0.5 indicate little or no consistent effect.}}{15}{table.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:delta_summary_flow}{{S9}{15}{Posterior summaries of $\Delta $ ($S^+ - S^-$) for inflorescence production across precipitation quantiles (mm, 5\%, 25\%, 50\%, 75\%, 100\%) for each species and herbivore treatment. Positive median values indicate beneficial effects of symbionts; negative medians indicate costly effects. $P(\Delta >0)$ quantifies the strength of evidence: values near 1 indicate strong support for a benefit, values near 0 indicate strong support for a cost, and values near 0.5 indicate little or no consistent effect}{table.caption.9}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S10}{\ignorespaces Posterior summaries of $\Delta $ ($S^+ - S^-$) for spikelet production across precipitation quantiles (mm, 5\%, 25\%, 50\%, 75\%, 100\%) for each species and herbivore treatment. Positive median values indicate beneficial effects of symbionts; negative medians indicate costly effects. $P(\Delta >0)$ quantifies the strength of evidence: values near 1 indicate strong support for a benefit, values near 0 indicate strong support for a cost, and values near 0.5 indicate little or no consistent effect.}}{16}{table.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:delta_summary_spike}{{S10}{16}{Posterior summaries of $\Delta $ ($S^+ - S^-$) for spikelet production across precipitation quantiles (mm, 5\%, 25\%, 50\%, 75\%, 100\%) for each species and herbivore treatment. Positive median values indicate beneficial effects of symbionts; negative medians indicate costly effects. $P(\Delta >0)$ quantifies the strength of evidence: values near 1 indicate strong support for a benefit, values near 0 indicate strong support for a cost, and values near 0.5 indicate little or no consistent effect}{table.caption.10}{}}
